<title>USA: Sherwin-Williams Q1 EPS $0.13 vs $0.11.</title>
<headline>Sherwin-Williams Q1 EPS $0.13 vs $0.11.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Sherwin-Williams Company and Subsidiaries</p>
<p>Statements of Consolidated Income (Unaudited)</p>
<p>							Three months ended</p>
<p>								March 31,</p>
<p> Thousands of dollars, except per share data.  1997     1996</p>
<p> Net sales				    $1,069,787     $857,771</p>
<p>Costs and expenses:</p>
<p>   Operating expenses			1,014,049	819,937</p>
<p>   Interest expense			     20,798	  5,436</p>
<p>   Interest and net investment income    (2,960)	(1,597)</p>
<p>   Other						(25)	  2,393</p>
<p>   Total					 1,031,862	826,169</p>
<p> Income before income taxes		   37,925	 31,602</p>
<p> Income taxes				     14,791	 12,009</p>
<p> Net income					 23,134	 19,593</p>
<p> Net income per share			     0.13	   0.11</p>
<p>Average shares and equivalents outstanding</p>
<p>						 172,335,790  172,395,202</p>
<p>The financial results for the three months ended March 31, 1997 include the results of operations of Thompson Minwax Holding Corp , acquired in Jan 1997, and other smaller acquisitions acquired at various times since the first quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>Excluding the results of operations of these acquisitions and the related costs of financing, the purchases from the first quarter of 1997, sales increased to $907,604,000 and earnings per share increased to $.13 per share.</p>
</text>
